    `I caused the assailant's death` IS TRUE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `my death or another's`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS FALSE

`killing an attacker who threatened only a slap` MEANS `My defence` WITH
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS TRUE
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS TRUE
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS FALSE
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS FALSE
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS TRUE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `some lesser harm`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS FALSE

`still hitting him after a police patrol arrived` MEANS `My defence` WITH
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS TRUE
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS TRUE
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS TRUE
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS FALSE
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS FALSE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `my death or another's`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS FALSE

`still hitting him after he ran off` MEANS `My defence` WITH
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS TRUE
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS FALSE
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS FALSE
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS FALSE
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS FALSE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `some lesser harm`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS FALSE

`breaking his arm to stop a shove` MEANS `My defence` WITH
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS TRUE
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS TRUE
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS FALSE
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS TRUE
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS FALSE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `some lesser harm`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS FALSE

`resisting a plain-clothes officer's good-faith arrest` MEANS `My defence` WITH
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS TRUE
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS TRUE
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS FALSE
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS FALSE
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS FALSE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `some lesser harm`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS TRUE

`resisting an officer I reasonably believed would cause grievous hurt` MEANS `My defence` WITH
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS TRUE
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS TRUE
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS FALSE
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS FALSE
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS FALSE
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS `grievous hurt`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS TRUE

§ `ss 82, 83 -- age`

#ASSERT `Is what I did no offence because of my age` 9 FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I did no offence because of my age` 11 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is what I did no offence because of my age` 11 TRUE

§ `ss 23 to 25 -- dishonestly and fraudulently`

#ASSERT `Did I act dishonestly` `intending wrongful gain`
#ASSERT NOT `Did I act dishonestly` `taking what I am entitled to`
#ASSERT NOT `Did I act dishonestly` `dishonest by ordinary standards but not knowing it`

#ASSERT NOT `Did I act fraudulently` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 378 to 381 -- theft`

#ASSERT `Have I committed theft` `cutting down a neighbour's tree and carrying it off`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed theft` `pulling at a neighbour's rooted tree without severing it`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed theft` `taking a ring found lying on the high road`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed theft` `taking back my watch from a jeweller I owe nothing`
#ASSERT `Have I committed theft` `taking back my pawned watch without repaying the loan`

#ASSERT `Which sections can punish my theft` `pocketing a phone from a shop counter` EQUALS (LIST `section 379`)
#ASSERT `Which sections can punish my theft` `stealing a parked car` EQUALS (LIST `section 379`, `section 379A`)
#ASSERT `Which sections can punish my theft` `a domestic servant stealing from the employer's flat` EQUALS (LIST `section 379`, `section 380`, `section 381`)

#ASSERT `Will I be disqualified from holding a driving licence` `section 379A` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Will I be disqualified from holding a driving licence` `section 379A` TRUE

§ `ss 415 to 420 -- cheating`

#ASSERT NOT `Have I cheated` `taking an advance for pepper I meant to deliver, then not delivering`
#ASSERT `Have I cheated` `deceiving someone into handing over property, fraudulently but not dishonestly`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I cheated` `a deception for an advantage too slight to complain of`

#ASSERT `Which section punishes my cheating` `selling a fake branded bag face to face` EQUALS (JUST `section 420(1)`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes my cheating` `selling a fake branded bag through an online marketplace` EQUALS (JUST `section 420(2)`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes my cheating` `selling it by a method the Minister has declared not remote communication` EQUALS (JUST `section 420(1)`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes my cheating` `deceiving a rival into missing a job interview` EQUALS (JUST `section 417`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes my cheating` `deceiving someone into handing over property, fraudulently but not dishonestly` EQUALS (JUST `section 417`)

§ `ss 319 to 335 -- hurt`

#ASSERT `Is the hurt I caused grievous` `a beating that kept someone from work for 21 days`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the hurt I caused grievous` `a beating that kept someone from work for 19 days`

#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `a slap that stings` EQUALS (JUST `section 323`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `a punch that causes a fall and permanent paralysis` EQUALS (JUST `section 323A`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `breaking someone's arm on purpose` EQUALS (JUST `section 325`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `slashing someone with a knife, leaving cuts` EQUALS (JUST `section 324`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `stabbing someone meaning to maim, breaking a rib` EQUALS (JUST `section 326`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `swinging a bottle meaning minor hurt, costing an eye` EQUALS (JUST `section 324`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `meaning to break a jaw, leaving only bruises` EQUALS (JUST `section 323`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `a blow on grave and sudden provocation, leaving bruises` EQUALS (JUST `section 334`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `a blow on provocation causing an unintended fracture` EQUALS (JUST `section 334A`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `breaking the provoker's nose on purpose` EQUALS (JUST `section 335`)
#ASSERT `Which section punishes the hurt I caused` `an accidental bump in a crowd` EQUALS NOTHING

